Import a snapshot from a QCOW2 file stored in Object Storage.

USAGE:
  scw instance snapshot import-from-object-storage [arg=value ...]

EXAMPLES:
  Import a snapshot from a QCOW2 file in Object Storage
    scw instance snapshot import-from-object-storage zone=fr-par-1 name=imported-snapshot bucket=my-bucket object-key=my-qcow2-file-name volume-type=l_ssd

ARGS:
  [project-id]          Project ID to use. If none is passed the default project ID will be used
  [name]                Name of the snapshot
  [tags.{index}]        Tags associated with the snapshot
  [bucket]              Object Storage bucket name
  [object-key]          Object key
  [size]                Size of the imported snapshot in bytes
  [volume-type=l_ssd]   Volume type of the snapshot (unknown_volume_type | l_ssd)
  [zone=fr-par-1]       Zone to target. If none is passed will use default zone from the config (fr-par-1 | fr-par-2 | fr-par-3 | nl-ams-1 | nl-ams-2 | nl-ams-3 | pl-waw-1 | pl-waw-2 | pl-waw-3 | it-mil-1)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for import-from-object-storage
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers       Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
      --web              open console page for the current resource
